// hosted content server's TERMS_URL is this page and its TERMS_VERSION is `version`. Any change to
// the text is a new version: change `version` here and TERMS_VERSION together, so everyone is asked
// to accept again.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';

const version = '2026-11-11';
---

<Page title="CMO Kit closed beta terms">
  <h1>CMO Kit closed beta terms</h1>
  <p>Version {version}</p>

  <h2>1. What these terms cover</h2>
  <p>These Closed Beta Terms ("Beta Terms") govern your access to and use of the CMO Kit closed beta (the "Beta"), provided by Growth Science LLC ("we", "us").</p>
  <p>By accepting these Beta Terms at sign-in, you agree to them. If you use CMO Kit for a business, you confirm you can accept them for that business.</p>

  <h2>2. Joining the waitlist is not access</h2>
  <p>Joining the waitlist only adds you to a list. It does not give you access to the Beta, and we do not promise that you will be invited. We choose who to invite, when, and in what order, at our sole discretion. Access starts only when we activate your account and you accept these Beta Terms.</p>

  <h2>3. It's a beta</h2>
  <p>The Beta is a pre-release version of a product we intend to sell. It may be incomplete, contain bugs, run slowly, or stop working. Features may change, be limited, or be removed at any time, with or without notice. We do not guarantee uptime, support response times, or any service level.</p>

  <h2>4. Free now, paid later</h2>
  <p>Access to the Beta is free unless we tell you otherwise in writing. We plan to offer CMO Kit as a paid product. We may end free access, introduce fees, or change prices at any time. We will give you at least 30 days' notice before you are charged anything, and you will not be charged unless you choose to continue on a paid plan. Pricing during or after the Beta may differ from any price we have mentioned before.</p>

  <h2>5. Ending or suspending access</h2>
  <p>We may suspend or end your access to the Beta, or end the Beta for everyone, at any time and for any reason. You may stop using the Beta at any time. Sections 6 through 10 survive the end of your access.</p>

  <h2>6. Your content and data</h2>
  <p>You keep ownership of the content you bring to CMO Kit, such as brand materials, footage, copy and campaign data ("Your Content"). You give us a limited license to host, process and display Your Content only to provide the Beta to you.</p>
  <p>During the Beta, data may be lost, reset or migrated. Keep your own copies of anything important. When we end the Beta or your access, we will give you a way to export Your Content, except where the law requires us to keep it.</p>

  <h2>7. Connected accounts</h2>
  <p>The Beta may connect to third-party services you authorize, such as Instagram, PostHog or Google. Your use of those services is governed by their own terms. You are responsible for what you publish on your own accounts. CMO Kit prepares content for your review, and you decide what gets posted.</p>

  <h2>8. Feedback</h2>
  <p>If you send us feedback, ideas or suggestions about CMO Kit, we may use them for any purpose without obligation to you.</p>

  <h2>9. Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>The Beta and anything we share with you about it that is not public is confidential. Please don't publish screenshots, benchmarks or details of unreleased features without our permission.</p>

